=4 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ r(r-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\,4\\le z\\le 7\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x^{2} + y^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da30d8b-b4d8-596a-8c80-6b14e0374096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536987} {:answer/id #uuid "0e208e2f-cf97-52a6-913e-893119de1c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536988} {:answer/id #uuid "20ec8899-9f98-5939-b1be-717c8a36b84e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{4}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536994} {:answer/id #uuid "37eefddf-45ba-5950-8013-940c638fd35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{7}^{4}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537007} {:answer/id #uuid "9f831628-be52-5b60-9299-337a30d46fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e208e2f-cf97-52a6-913e-893119de1c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536988} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b7df119-1e10-5a12-b44e-c332dcfb8b0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69ed0333-f7ae-5aef-adf8-ef1e138c3825" :question/problem "If the solid region $R$ is given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 16,y\\ge 0,\\,4\\le z\\le 7\\},\n$$\n\nthen express the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x^{2} + y^{2}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nas an equivalent integral in cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/80/80a919b28ae7ed559b06b34bd8512859794a7d6550970b56347e2deb653bf76d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-half of a right vertical cylinder of radius $4$ whose axis passes through the point $(4,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=4,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=7.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2}=16$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta-4)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2} & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta+16+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ r(r-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\,4\\le z\\le 7\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x^{2} + y^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e702de4-81fb-57f8-b700-52c7a2d5b037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}^{-1}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537029} {:answer/id #uuid "6eef909b-2ae7-54ad-8347-4b8012df300a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537030} {:answer/id #uuid "a4798cdd-ba94-5538-b8db-9acc2dd4aebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537046} {:answer/id #uuid "d2013466-8cd9-50cf-ab08-7466182070c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537061} {:answer/id #uuid "f189cf4d-34b4-53e8-8fda-d1dc11be310f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r^{2}}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6eef909b-2ae7-54ad-8347-4b8012df300a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537030} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e63057c-fad2-57b0-ab28-4c0735601f0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536991}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a4d1aae-ff57-5336-93e6-e2feb480e2e3" :question/problem "If the solid region $R$ is given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4,\\,-1\\le z\\le x + 5\\},\n$$\n\nthen express the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2} + 2}}\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nas an equivalent integral in cylindrical polar coordinates." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/f8/f830c1469527c615d213ffcd11e472083c77d7e5fbc8c1577a85244fb5739fc4.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(-2,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=-1,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=x + 5=r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's write the equation $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta+2)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta+4+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}+4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ r(r+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire circle, we must have $r=- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le - 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3 \\pi}{2},\\,-1\\le z\\le r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2} + 2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2}+2}}\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+2}}\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0525826c-a736-5227-9f0a-27dd1c50c845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-4}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536984} {:answer/id #uuid "202eb17e-51e1-5247-9d96-d74c13ad2578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-4}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}\\frac{r^{2}}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536992} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfe631f-2545-5c41-af46-41c806290c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}^{-4}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537060